{% comment %}
  <option> list of UPCOMING seminars, for a bundle's "which seminar" select.

  Usage:
    {% render 'suf-seminar-options', events: section.settings.events_collection %}

  Takes a collection. Emits nothing at all if it is blank or empty, so a caller
  can test for that and skip rendering the whole field.

  THE FIRST OPTION IS "I'll choose later", AND IT IS THE DEFAULT. That is the
  point of the field rather than a fallback for an empty list.

  A seminar is a trip: flights, a hotel, a free weekend. Asking someone to
  commit to a date at the moment they finally decide to buy inserts a
  travel-planning decision into a checkout, and the likely outcome is not a
  wrong date -- it is a closed tab. So the seminar is sold as a CREDIT and
  booked afterwards; picking now is an affordance for people who already know.

  It also makes the field work unchanged for a package carrying three seminar
  credits, where asking up front is not merely awkward but unanswerable.

  SHARES ITS FILTERING WITH sections/suf-semlist.liquid, deliberately, because
  the two must never disagree: a seminar offered here that the seminars page
  has dropped is a booking nobody can honour.

  Two things in that logic are load-bearing and are the reason this is a
  snippet rather than copied Liquid:

  1. `| plus: 0` on BOTH sides of the date comparison. Liquid compares strings
     with `<` by silently returning false, so an unconverted filter never drops
     anything and looks correct right up until a date passes.
  2. The `YYYYMMDD~index` sort key. Liquid cannot sort a collection by a
     metafield -- `sort` reaches simple properties only -- so the order is
     built by sorting zero-padded fixed-width strings, which sort lexically in
     date order. The INDEX is carried rather than the handle because
     `all_products` is capped at 20 lookups a page.

  Metafield keys are `custom.seminar_*`. They were `custom.custom_seminar_*`
  until 2026-09-02 -- a definition's Name had been typed as "custom.seminar_x"
  and Shopify slugged the key from it inside the namespace it already had.
  Renamed at source, so nothing carries the doubling now.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  LABEL is read in the closed select, which clips rather than wraps: keep it
  under ~36 characters. VALUE goes to the order, where staff read it weeks
  later, so it names what is outstanding.

  NOT BLANK: Shopify drops a blank property, and a seminar bundle with no
  Seminar line cannot be told apart from one where the picker failed.

  Cost: with JS blocked, a two-certification order carries this line
  spuriously. The Selection property above it contradicts it visibly.
{%- endcomment -%}
<option value="Credit — to be booked later" selected>Choose later — use my credit</option>

{%- if events != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign keyed = ''
    for p in events.products
      assign starts = p.metafields.custom.seminar_start.value | date: '%Y%m%d'
      if starts == blank
        assign starts = '99999999'
      endif
      assign keyed = keyed | append: starts | append: '~' | append: forloop.index0 | append: ','
    endfor
    assign keys = keyed | split: ',' | sort
  -%}

  {%- for key in keys -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign idx = key | split: '~' | last | plus: 0
      assign seminar = events.products[idx]

      assign starts = seminar.metafields.custom.seminar_start.value
      assign ends = seminar.metafields.custom.seminar_end.value | default: starts

      # Judged on the END date, so a two-day seminar is still bookable on its
      # first morning -- same rule the seminars page applies.
      assign over = ends | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
      assign is_past = false
      if ends != blank and over < today
        assign is_past = true
      endif

      # Each half formatted on its own line. Chaining them pipes the whole
      # concatenated string into `date`, not the end date.
      assign m1 = starts | date: '%B'
      assign m2 = ends | date: '%B'
      assign first_half = starts | date: '%B %-d'
      if m1 == m2
        assign second_half = ends | date: '%-d'
      else
        assign second_half = ends | date: '%B %-d'
      endif
    -%}

    {%- unless is_past -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Same "Tampa, FL" the event row shows, from the same snippet. This
        string ends up on the ORDER, so a picker naming a city the seminars
        page names differently would be two names for one booking.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture city -%}
        {%- render 'suf-seminar-place', product: seminar -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign city = city | strip -%}

      {%- capture label -%}
        {{- city | default: seminar.title -}}
        {%- if starts != blank %} · {{ first_half }}
          {%- if second_half != blank and second_half != first_half %}–{{ second_half }}{% endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      <option value="{{ label | strip | escape }}">{{ label | strip }}</option>
    {%- endunless -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
